SUSPECTED BUG: top-down, the CLI's entry point (large, -fanout=2): a switch over 11 commands, each returning the
set of a different use case. Correct set: errUsage bare and behind "%w (unknown command %q)", parse.Line's set,
and the sets of Transfer, Balance (behind "cli: balance: %w"), Owner, batch, Explain, Preview, settled, SetStatus,
check, Ready and PublishFirst; the deferred io.Copy / store.Close cannot change the unnamed result.
Actual: 87 entries that all come from the first case (parse.Line and Service.Transfer) plus bare errUsage, and one
unresolved(fixpoint-limit) "result 0 of run can carry more than 1024 values". Everything else is cut: no
"cli: balance: %w", no "%w (unknown command %q)", no ErrUnsupported, NotFoundError[TransferID], ErrTxDone, rule or
event-handler origin. The cut is announced, but the 1024 values are used up by the combinations of
errors.Join(err, aerr) in Service.Transfer (see service_transfer_decl), so an entry point with about 300 distinct
origins degrades to an arbitrary prefix.
-- args --
-fanout=2 cmd/cli/main.go:@run
